      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240477",
      ":question/problem": "The lines $l$ and $m$ intersect and form a linear pair of two congruent angles $\u22201$ and $\u22202$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The lines $m$ and $l$ are perpendicular.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u22201\u2245\u22202$ | Given |\n| 2 | $m\u22201 = m\u22202$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | $\u22201$ and $\u22202$ are supplementary | Linear pair postulate |\n| 4 | $m\u22201 + m\u22202 = 180^{\u2218}$ | Definition of supplementary angles |\n| 5 | $m\u22201 + m\u22201 = 180^{\u2218}$ | Substitution |\n| 6 | $m\u22201 = 90^{\u2218}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 7 | The lines $m$ and $l$ are perpendicular | {{field-3}} |"
    },
