      ":question/problem": "![](images/cd/cdf0c67aede5833f6426bc8531b73613eab17db03cec20eaa63c993aee1cbf10.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $l\u22a5m$ and $a\u22a5b$\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u22201\u2245\u22202$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $l\u22a5m$ | Given |\n| 2 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $a\u22a5b$ | Given |\n| 4 | $m\u22202 = 90^{\u2218}$ | Definition of perpendicular lines |\n| 5 | $90^{\u2218} = m\u22202$ | Symmetric property of equality |\n| 6 | $m\u22201 = m\u22202$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 7 | $\u22201\u2245\u22202$ | {{field-4}} |"
